  Will AI lead to layoffs? Are people already losing their jobs to AI? While overall unemployment in the U.S. is still [relatively low](https://www.bls.gov/charts/employment-situation/civilian-unemployment-rate.htm), there is [considerable speculation](https://fortune.com/2025/08/08/ai-layoffs-jobs-market-shrinks-entry-level/) that the adoption of generative AI was a cause of recent layoffs and slowed hiring, particularly in the [tech industry](https://fortune.com/2026/01/22/despite-promises-ai-create-more-jobs-1-2-million-jobs-actually-slashed-last-year/), for [entry-level workers](https://finance.yahoo.com/news/two-thirds-companies-slow-entry-110000876.html), and in [customer service and programming jobs](https://digitaleconomy.stanford.edu/app/uploads/2025/11/CanariesintheCoalMine_Nov25.pdf). More may be coming: Leading CEOs—including those from Ford, Amazon, Salesforce, and JP Morgan Chase—have proclaimed that many white-collar jobs at their companies will soon disappear.
  
