  ## Topline
  
  Meta is will layoff 10% of its workforce, the company told employees in a memo Thursday, and won't hire workers for 6,000 open jobs in hopes of offsetting the money it's spending to integrate artificial intelligence into the company in the latest corporate shakeup blamed on AI this year.
  
  ![Big Tech CEOs Testify At Senate Judiciary Committee Hearing](https://imageio.forbes.com/specials-images/imageserve/69ea6ea39fcb4e1c82ad1ae2/Big-Tech-CEOs-Testify-At-Senate-Judiciary-Committee-Hearing/0x0.jpg?format=jpg&crop=3744,2107,x0,y0,safe&width=1440)
  
  Meta CEO and billionaire Mark Zuckerberg.
  
  Getty Images
  
  ## Timeline
  
  APRIL 23, 2026Meta’s announced job cuts, roughly **8,000** scheduled for May 20, are part of a plan initially reported by [Reuters](https://www.reuters.com/business/world-at-work/meta-planning-sweeping-layoffs-ai-costs-mount-2026-03-14/ "https://www.reuters.com/business/world-at-work/meta-planning-sweeping-layoffs-ai-costs-mount-2026-03-14/") to layoff what could amount to more than 20% of the company (which employs [roughly](https://finance.yahoo.com/news/cramer-why-does-meta-78-111800491.html "https://finance.yahoo.com/news/cramer-why-does-meta-78-111800491.html") 75,000 people) as it invests in AI and plans to utilize AI-assisted workers.
  
  APRIL 15, 2026Billionaire [Evan Spiegel](https://www.forbes.com/profile/evan-spiegel/?list=rtb&ctpv=rtb "https://www.forbes.com/profile/evan-spiegel/?list=rtb&ctpv=rtb") told employees of [Snap](https://deadline.com/2026/04/snap-layoffs-ceo-evan-spiegel-ai-1236861335/ "https://deadline.com/2026/04/snap-layoffs-ceo-evan-spiegel-ai-1236861335/"), the parent company of social media app Snapchat, that **1,000** jobs would be cut because “rapid advancements in artificial intelligence” will allow the same work to be done by a smaller group of people. The move is expected to save the company $500 million by the second half of 2026.
  
  MARCH 31, 2026 [Oracle](https://www.cnbc.com/2026/03/31/oracle-layoffs-ai-spending.html "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/03/31/oracle-layoffs-ai-spending.html"), founded by billionaire [Larry Ellison](https://www.forbes.com/profile/larry-ellison/ "https://www.forbes.com/profile/larry-ellison/"), is cutting **20,000 to 30,000** employees as the company heavily invests in building out AI infrastructure.
  
  MARCH 25, 2026 Meta, led by the world's fifth-richest-person [Mark Zuckerberg](https://www.forbes.com/profile/mark-zuckerberg/?list=rtb&ctpv=rtb "https://www.forbes.com/profile/mark-zuckerberg/?list=rtb&ctpv=rtb"), laid off **700** people, the New York Times reported, in cuts that "underline how much A.I. has changed the tech industry."
  
  MARCH 19, 2026Crypto.com laid off 12%, or about **180**, of its employees as it integrates "enterprise-wide AI," with CEO Kris Marszalek [explaining](https://www.cnbc.com/2026/03/19/crypto-com-layoffs-12percent-ai-job-loss.html "https://www.cnbc.com/2026/03/19/crypto-com-layoffs-12percent-ai-job-loss.html") the jobs that were cut were "roles that do not adapt in our new world."
  
  MARCH 11, 2026Software company [Atlassian](https://www.atlassian.com/blog/announcements/atlassian-team-update-march-2026 "https://www.atlassian.com/blog/announcements/atlassian-team-update-march-2026") cut roughly 10% of its workforce— **1,600** people—in order to “self-fund further investment in AI,” with co-founder Mike Cannon-Brookes saying he "fundamentally believes people and AI create the best outcomes.”
  
  FEB. 26, 2026Block, billionaire [Jack Dorsey](https://www.forbes.com/profile/jack-dorsey/?list=rtb&ctpv=rtb "https://www.forbes.com/profile/jack-dorsey/?list=rtb&ctpv=rtb")'s company, [cut](https://x.com/jack/status/2027129697092731343 "https://x.com/jack/status/2027129697092731343") more than **4,000** jobs (almost half the company’s staff) in a major restructuring to integrate AI and create smaller, faster teams.
  
  FEB. 25, 2026Software company [WiseTech Global](https://www.reuters.com/business/world-at-work/australias-wisetech-global-plans-2000-job-cuts-amid-ai-overhaul-2026-02-24/ "https://www.reuters.com/business/world-at-work/australias-wisetech-global-plans-2000-job-cuts-amid-ai-overhaul-2026-02-24/") said it’s eliminating about one-third of employees ( **2,000** jobs) over the next two years to restructure around artificial intelligence.
  
  FEB. 9, 2026 It was [first reported](https://www.businessinsider.com/salesforce-cuts-jobs-executive-changes-2026-2 "https://www.businessinsider.com/salesforce-cuts-jobs-executive-changes-2026-2") that Salesforce laid off fewer than **1,000** people in marketing, product management, data analytics and the company's Agentforce AI product at the start of the year, cuts that came about six months after Salesforce CEO and [billionaire](https://www.forbes.com/profile/marc-benioff/?list=rtb&ctpv=rtb "https://www.forbes.com/profile/marc-benioff/?list=rtb&ctpv=rtb") Marc Benioff [blamed AI](https://www.cnbc.com/2025/09/02/salesforce-ceo-confirms-4000-layoffs-because-i-need-less-heads-with-ai.html "https://www.cnbc.com/2025/09/02/salesforce-ceo-confirms-4000-layoffs-because-i-need-less-heads-with-ai.html") for axing 4,000 support staff jobs.
  
  JAN. 27, 2026 Social media platform [Pinterest](https://www.reuters.com/business/world-at-work/pinterest-cuts-nearly-15-jobs-redirect-resources-ai-2026-01-27/ "https://www.reuters.com/business/world-at-work/pinterest-cuts-nearly-15-jobs-redirect-resources-ai-2026-01-27/") said it would cut about 15% of its workforce (about **800** people based on a headcount of 5,200 at the end of 2025) to reallocate money toward AI-focused roles, sending its stock tumbling nearly 10%.
  
