  Mass Layoffs in 2026 are skyrocketing. The layoff story most Americans are reading in 2026 is wrong, and that's the reason people are getting blindsided. The 2023 mass cuts were one-time corrections. The 2026 pattern is rolling small-batch cuts every Friday, funded by share buybacks and AI capex reallocation, hitting the L3-to-L5 middle of the org chart while leaving entry-level and executive roles relatively intact. In this video we walk through the Challenger Gray data, the corporate earnings transcripts that called the shift, the specific roles that AI is now replacing at the task level, and the framework to know whether your role is structurally protected or quietly on the list. If you are working in any analyst, coordinator, or project-management capacity, this is the breakdown you need before your next 1-on-1.
  
  1\. If 60 percent of Fortune 500 companies are reporting hiring slowdowns in Q1 2026, why is the unemployment rate not yet reflecting it?
  2\. Why are tech companies cutting 200 people every Friday instead of the 10,000-at-a-time announcements of 2023?
  3\. What does it mean for the American middle class when the org chart loses its middle?
  
