  The year 2026 is adding even more momentum to significant changes AI is already causing to the job market.
  
  As AI tools become increasingly powerful, and with highly anticipated LLM models like OpenAI's GPT-6 likely to be launching this year, more people are at risk of having their job fully automated.
  
  Dubbed the Godfather of AI, Geoffrey Hinton has predicted the technology will gain the capabilities to replace "many, many jobs" in 2026.
  
  And Manus, dubbed the first general-purpose AI agent, was acquired by Meta for $2 billion in December 2025.
  
  However, will AI really put most people’s jobs at risk, or is the reality more nuanced?
  
